\PYG{c+cm}{/* \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{} 4 · processing state: who analysed this, if anyone \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{} */}
\PYG{c+cm}{/* The page reports what the instrument\PYGZsq{}s own software concluded, so the first question}
\PYG{c+cm}{   about any file is who produced the results in it. Four states, discriminated by what the}
\PYG{c+cm}{   file itself says \PYGZhy{} never by the file name:}

\PYG{c+cm}{     instrument     a vendor container (.ixo / .eds): the instrument\PYGZsq{}s own record}
\PYG{c+cm}{     vendor\PYGZhy{}export  an RDML exported from the vendor\PYGZsq{}s software: it names an \PYGZlt{}instrument\PYGZgt{},}
\PYG{c+cm}{                    carries Cq, and no re\PYGZhy{}analysis tool is named anywhere in it}
\PYG{c+cm}{     third\PYGZhy{}party    an RDML whose results were computed by another tool: \PYGZlt{}ampEffMet\PYGZgt{} names}
\PYG{c+cm}{                    it, or \PYGZlt{}backgroundDeterminationMethod\PYGZgt{} does}
\PYG{c+cm}{     raw            an RDML with fluorescence and no Cq at all: nobody has analysed it}

\PYG{c+cm}{   Measured on the corpus:}
\PYG{c+cm}{     2026\PYGZhy{}06\PYGZhy{}15\PYGZus{}RAS\PYGZus{}FFPE.rdml   instrument \PYGZdq{}QuantStudio Dx\PYGZdq{}, bg \PYGZdq{}Background Subtraction\PYGZdq{} \PYGZhy{}\PYGZgt{} vendor\PYGZhy{}export}
\PYG{c+cm}{     example\PYGZus{}3\PYGZus{}linregpcr.rdml   no instrument, bg \PYGZdq{}LinRegPCR, constant\PYGZdq{}, ampEffMet LinRegPCR \PYGZhy{}\PYGZgt{} third\PYGZhy{}party}
\PYG{c+cm}{     example\PYGZus{}1\PYGZus{}raw.rdml         no provenance, no Cq \PYGZhy{}\PYGZgt{} raw                                                */}
